  $ tt backup verify --backup-storage=file:///var/backups --format json

=== tt backup-id --help
Print an identifier for a new backup: the current UTC time as
20060102T150405Z, followed by a newline. Pass it as is to --backup-id of
'tt backup start', 'tt backup upload' and 'tt backup finalize'.

Identifiers sort as text in the order they are generated, which is the order
'tt backup upload' requires. The command exits once the second it printed is
over, so the next call prints a later one.

That holds for calls made one after another on one host. Calls running at the
same time, calls on different hosts, or a clock stepped back can print the same
identifier; generate one per backup run and hand it to every step.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt backup-id [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
  -h, --help   help for backup-id

=== tt binary --help
Manage tt and tt Enterprise, Tarantool Community and Enterprise, TCM,
and SDK bundles.

Use --scope to choose where binaries are managed:
  project (default): .tarantool/ in the project directory: the current
    directory or its nearest parent with app.manifest.toml,
    .templates/<name>/instances.yaml or .templates/<name>/config.yaml; the
    current directory outside a project.
  user: $TT_USER_ROOT when set; otherwise
    Linux: $XDG_DATA_HOME/tarantool when XDG_DATA_HOME is an absolute path;
      otherwise ~/.local/share/tarantool.
    macOS: ~/Library/Application Support/tarantool.
  system: $TT_SYSTEM_ROOT when set; otherwise
    Linux: /opt/tarantool.
    macOS: /Library/Application Support/tarantool.
TT_USER_ROOT and TT_SYSTEM_ROOT must be absolute paths.

Each scope stores executables directly in
<root>/versions/<product>/<product>_<version>/, with Tarantool headers in
include/tarantool.
Active executables are linked from <root>/bin/, and active Tarantool headers
from <root>/include/tarantool.

Tarantool CE and EE keep separate versions and share the active Tarantool links.
tt and tt-ee keep separate versions and share the active tt executable.

For project installations, run "source .env/activate.sh" in the project
directory to activate the installed binaries.

SDK installations select Tarantool Enterprise, tt Enterprise, TCM, and headers
together.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
