=== tt binary switch --help
Switch to an installed version in the selected scope.
Without arguments, choose the program and version interactively. With only
a program, choose its version. For tarantool and tt, choose the edition first,
then
one of its installed versions. CE and EE share the active Tarantool binary
and headers. tt and tt-ee share the active tt executable.

Bare Tarantool and tt versions select CE; append ce or ee to choose an edition
explicitly. Tarantool Enterprise build names and sdk-<bundle-version> select EE.

Switching tarantool-sdk (also sdk and SDK) selects all of its components and
headers together. Use sdk-<bundle-version> to select an individual SDK
component.

For tarantool-ee, tt-ee, and tcm, X.Y.Z must match a single installed version in
the
selected scope.
If multiple builds match, the command reports their full names and requires
an unambiguous choice before changing the active version.
Use a full installed version name to select a specific build.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt binary switch [program] [version] [flags]

  tt binary switch [program] [version] [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
  -h, --help   help for switch
[0;1;39m
GLOBAL FLAGS[0m
      --scope string   Scope: project, user or system (default "project")
  -V, --verbose        Show diagnostic output and build commands
[0;1;39m
EXAMPLES[0m
  # Choose a program and version interactively.
  $ tt binary switch --scope project

  # Choose a Tarantool version interactively.
  $ tt binary switch tarantool --scope project

  # Switch to a specific Tarantool version.
  $ tt binary switch tarantool 3.0.0 --scope project

