=== tt instance --help
Start, stop and inspect the instances of an application on this host.

A target is <APP>:<INSTANCE>, every instance of an application <APP>:*, a
comma-separated list of them, or none, which is every instance of the project
the command runs in. An application is looked for in the project the command
runs in when the project has its name, and in the system scope otherwise;
--scope project, user or system picks the scope outright. The instances are
those of the pair of the application: the host's <root>/etc/<app>/, or the
template .templates/<template>/ of the application, "default" unless --template
names another.

A command that acts on several instances goes on after a failure of one of them
and exits 3 when it failed for some of them only. What the exit codes mean is in
tt help errors.

An instance that tt service systemd install put under a systemd unit is started
and stopped with systemctl: start, stop, restart and kill refuse it, and status
shows its unit.

