=== tt package download --help
Fetch rock files from the configured servers into --dir and write the LuaRocks
manifest that indexes them, so the directory is itself a rock server: point
--registry or TT_REGISTRIES at it and the project builds with no network at all.
With no arguments the project's locked closure is mirrored at its exact versions
— every product's dependencies and the dev closure — which needs a lock, so run
tt package resolve first. A dependency that does not come from a registry has no
rock file to mirror and is skipped with a warning. Re-running overwrites and
re-indexes, so a mirror can be extended in place. Each written path is printed
to stdout.

