=== tt package install --help
Unpack a package archive into the chosen scope and bring the tree to a runnable
state. A with-deps archive is a plain offline extraction; a --without-deps one
is unpacked and its dependencies are refetched from the registry using the
lock's pins. The runtime a with-deps archive bundles (_runtime/) is installed
the way tt binary installs it, into versions/ of the scope root —
<root>/versions/ in the user and system scopes, .tarantool/versions/ in the
project — unless that version is there already. Several packages installed into
one project share a .rocks/ tree, so a dependency they lock at different
versions is reconciled to one both accept, or the install fails with an
explanation; a project that selects no tarantool yet gets the bundled one
selected in .tarantool/bin. In the user and system scopes the archive becomes
one version of an application, <root>/versions/<name>/<name>_<version>/, laid
out like a project next to what tt binary installs into the same root, and
<root>/apps/<name> is pointed at it: install activates the version it installed.
It runs on the tarantool its lock bundles, whatever <root>/bin/tarantool
selects. Versions live side by side; installing one that is already there needs
--force, which is refused while instances of the application run.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt package install ARCHIVE... [flags]

  tt package install ARCHIVE... [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
      --force          reinstall over an existing package or version
                       (destructive)
  -h, --help           help for install
      --locked         fail if the archive lock does not match its manifest
      --scope string   install scope: project (the working directory), user or
                       system (an application version under the root tt binary
                       uses) (default "project")
      --upgrade        install only when the archive version is higher than the
                       installed one (in user and system, than every installed
